00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:40,620
Scout Master Ship in seven minutes or less.

185
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:50,660
So, as I said, this is our final installment

186
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:52,620
in the steps to scout advancement.

187
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:56,060
There are four steps to scout advancement.

188
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,260
Number one is a scout learns.

189
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,980
Number two is a scout is tested.

190
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:03,660
Number three is a scout is reviewed.

191
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:06,980
And number four is a scout is recognized,

192
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:11,980
And we're going to be talking about that fourth step today.

193
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:14,540
Let's go to several of the resources that we have.

194
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:17,940
The first is the Guide to Advancement 2011..

195
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,820
And it has this to say. it says:

196
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:23,460
immediate recognition is a powerful incentive

197
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:26,980
of the Boy Scouts of America Advancement Program.

198
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:29,140
A scout should receive his new badge

199
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:31,300
as soon as possible after his achievement

200
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,980
has been certified by a board of review.

201
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:36,420
A simple ceremony at the conclusion of a troop meeting

202
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,460
or during a campout is ideal,

203
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:41,420
with the Scout Master making the presentation of the badge.

204
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,860
In addition, a troop holds a court of honor

205
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:46,460
every three months, a formal recognition

206
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:49,220
with families, friends and the public in attendance.

207
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:52,260
All scouts who have moved up to any rank

208
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:53,700
or who have earned merit badges

209
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:57,020
since the last court of honor should be recognized.

210
00:13:57,020 --> 00:14:00,699
The Scout Master Handbook echoes this when it says

211
00:14:00,699 --> 00:14:03,380
when the board of review has approved his advancement,

212
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:06,260
the scout deserves recognition as soon as possible.

213
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,740
This should be done at a ceremony

214
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,260
at the next unit meeting.

215
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:12,220
The certificate for his new rank may be presented later

216
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:14,060
during a formal court of honor.

217
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:16,060
The Guide to Advancement also notes

218
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:18,380
that the board of review date,

219
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:20,900
not the subsequent court of honor date,

220
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,660
becomes any rank's effective date.

221
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:29,180
So in cases where tenure starts being counted,

222
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:32,500
it starts being counted from the board of review date,

223
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:35,620
not the court of honor date but the board of review date.

224
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:39,140
The troop committee guidebook echoes the same directions.

225
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:40,540
It said when a scout advances

226
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,459
he should be recognized as soon as possible,

227
00:14:42,459 --> 00:14:44,900
preferably at the next unit meeting.

228
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,860
He has recognized a second time

229
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:49,620
at a public ceremony called a court of honor.

230
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,339
The main purposes of the court of honor

231
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,300
are to furnish formal recognition for advancement

232
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:57,180
and to provide incentive for scouts to advance.

233
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,980
Formal courts of honor should be conducted

234
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,780
at least four times a year.

235
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,380
All scouts who have advanced

236
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:05,260
since the previous court of honor are honored.

237
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:06,300
Their parents and friends

238
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:08,620
should be invited to attend the ceremony.

239
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,380
Suggestions on court of honor agendas and ceremonies

240
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:15,340
are found in troop program resources for Boy Scout leaders.

241
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:18,140
So after having read those resources

242
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:20,980
we see that in the fourth step of scout advancement

243
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,500
a scout is recognized twice.

244
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:27,180
He receives the badge or emblem as soon as possible

245
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:30,420
and he's also recognized at a court of honor.

246
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,980
As far as I can tell, every advancement award

247
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:36,860
offered by the Boy Scouts of America has two components:

248
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:38,860
There's the badge itself

249
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:42,740
and there's a certificate that goes along with the badge.

250
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:45,420
Now, that word certificate confused me

251
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:47,900
for a long time. as a young scout master

252
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,660
I was looking for a certificate

253
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:51,980
and what they're talking about is the little card

254
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,819
that comes along with the badge

255
00:15:53,819 --> 00:15:55,660
that usually the scout master

256
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:56,939
and the senior patrol leader sign

257
00:15:56,939 --> 00:15:58,219
when it's a rank advancement

258
00:15:58,219 --> 00:15:59,860
And for the higher ranks,

259
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:02,860
I think that there's even a signature slot there

260
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,140
for the troop committee chair.

261
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,900
What we are directed to do

262
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:11,140
is to present the badge as soon as possible

263
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,939
and then we hold on to the card

264
00:16:12,939 --> 00:16:16,100
or the certificate to present at a court of honor.

265
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,860
So a scout needs to get that badge

266
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,220
as soon as possible

267
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:23,860
after the achievement has been certified by border review

268
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:26,940
or we've recorded a merit badge or something like that.

269
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:28,540
Let's get him that badge right away,

270
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:30,060
let him sew it on his uniform,

271
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:31,940
let him put it on his merit badge sash.

272
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:34,900
I mean, the whole idea of this first presentation

273
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:36,860
is getting it to the scout.

274
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:39,180
He's earned it, it's been recorded properly

275
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:41,500
and we want him to have it as soon as possible.

276
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,940
There's no reason it needs to sit around

277
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:46,720
for weeks or months waiting to be distributed.

278
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:50,440
The Scout Master Handbook mentions a simple ceremony.

279
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:54,200
The way it works for us is that our advancement chairman

280
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:57,800
will give me the badge and the certificate

281
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:01,040
and I will hand the badge to the senior patrol leader

282
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:03,160
at the closing of our troop meeting

283
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,920
and I'll hold on to the certificate

284
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,800
so he can read the name.

285
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,160
The scout steps forward,

286
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,880
receives the badge with a handshake

287
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,440
from the senior patrol leader,

288
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:13,600
His fellow scouts give him a little round of applause

289
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,440
and that's it.

290
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,760
It's very, very simple.

291
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:17,240
You notice that it also mentioned

292
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,839
that you can do this at a camp out

293
00:17:18,839 --> 00:17:20,440
and that would be great.

294
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:23,760
Round of camp fire at camp out. very simple presentation

295
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:26,119
and noting. you know we're going to recognize this

296
00:17:26,119 --> 00:17:28,520
more formally at our next court of honor.

297
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,760
So that's the first time that a scout is recognized

298
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,500
when he gets that badge.

299
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:36,660
The second time is going to be a more formal recognition

300
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,920
at the court of honor,

301
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,640
Periodically, and every three months

302
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,360
is recommended in all the literature.

303
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:45,360
a formal court of honor is held to recognize ranks

304
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,280
and merit badges and any other achievements.

305
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:49,200
since the last court of honor,

306
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,480
I don't know of any official policy

307
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,560
or directions from the Boy Scouts of America

308
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:57,520
describing the way to hold a court of honor

309
00:17:57,520 --> 00:18:00,840
or any particular rules about what has to happen

310
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,360
at a court of honor.

311
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,880
You'll find lots and lots of suggestions

312
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:09,680
for courts of honor in the troop program resources guide

313
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:12,440
and these are of course suggestions.

314
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:15,840
These aren't necessarily directions or policy statements.

315
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:18,000
When a scouts completed his border review

316
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,960
and the paperwork has been signed,

317
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:23,340
he was moved from the next rank to another.

318
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:25,040
It's already happened.

319
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:28,320
A court of honor only recognizes that achievement,

320
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,720
It does not bestow the achievement,

321
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:32,920
And I think that's an important concept to note,

322
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:36,320
because the date of the border review

323
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:39,560
is the effective date of the award

324
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:42,240
and not the court of honor date.

325
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:46,800
If a scout becomes first class at his border review,

326
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,960
whatever the date of that border review was,

327
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:53,160
begins his tenure for star, and the same applies

328
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:58,160
to star and life as far as when the tenure officially begins

329
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:02,560
for fulfilling the tenure requirement for the next rank.

330
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:05,800
And while I don't run into this very often,

331
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:06,640
every once in a while,

332
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:09,320
somebody has the idea that a court of honor

333
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:13,399
is like a wedding ceremony or swearing in a public servant,

334
00:19:13,399 --> 00:19:17,600
where some combination of actions and words

335
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:20,159
actually changes a person's status

336
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:21,399
as a result of the ceremony.

337
00:19:21,399 --> 00:19:23,240
Courts of honor aren't like that.

338
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:25,919
Courts of honor are just recognitions

339
00:19:25,919 --> 00:19:27,879
of something that has already happened.

340
00:19:27,879 --> 00:19:31,919
Now, nearly every troop has their own specific way

341
00:19:31,919 --> 00:19:34,480
and their traditions surrounding a court of honor,

342
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,399
and I wouldn't ever say any of them

343
00:19:36,399 --> 00:19:38,360
were just flat out wrong.

344
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,360
I prefer some ways over others,

345
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:42,700
but that's just my personal preference.

346
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:45,980
So what follows are my own ideas

347
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,240
about the way things ought to be,

348
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,880
And so when we're listening to this,

349
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,960
remember from here on out:

350
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:53,160
this is just my opinion.

351
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:56,880
These are not policy statements or directives

352
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,240
given to us by the BSA. okay,

353
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:01,440
I think, first of all, that simplicity

354
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:04,400
and predictability and consistency

355
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,480
are three really important elements

356
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:07,920
of a good court of honor.

357
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:10,960
Simple, predictable ceremonies

358
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:13,160
that are presented consistently

359
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,560
have a lot to recommend them,

360
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,640
and I think that they really help our scouts

361
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:19,300
appreciate exactly what's going on.

362
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:22,200
If we choose a ceremony and we kind of stick to it,

363
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:24,200
scouts are going to be familiar with it.

364
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:28,320
There's going to be fewer terrified, vacant stares

365
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:31,500
from whoever's presenting awards

366
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,560
and whoever's emceeing the ceremony

367
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:36,120
and there'll be a lot less uncertain

368
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:38,920
kind of wandering around and shuffling of feet.

369
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:40,920
And if you've been to several different courts of honor,

370
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:43,040
you probably understand exactly what I mean.

371
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,840
I think it's good that awards

372
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:47,920
are presented the same way over time

373
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:51,760
So there's a consistent recognition of the same award

374
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,240
from one year to the next. for all the scouts,

375
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,360
Merit badges are presented the same way,

376
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:59,160
badges of rank are presented the same way,

377
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,720
and that that consistency sends a message

378
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:05,000
that everyone's achievement is weighted the same

379
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,200
and it means the same thing.

380
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:12,200
Repetition also brings home the messages of the ceremony.

381
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,880
If we change the ceremony up every single time,

382
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:18,840
in my opinion, I think we end up missing some things.

383
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:22,560
I can also see the virtue in different ways

384
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:26,000
of saying things, but I stick them with the idea

385
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,380
that the repetition helps bring home the message.

386
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:32,680
And simplicity, finally, means brevity.

387
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:38,080
Let's keep the audience interested and engaged.

388
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:41,520
Let's not let these things drag on a whole lot

389
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:44,520
and have a lot of extemporaneous talking

390
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:45,680
and things like that.

391
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:48,160
Let's keep them brief.

392
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:51,880
We've used the same basic court of honor script,

393
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:55,600
with a few changes, for probably about 20 years or so.

394
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:57,800
You'll find all manner of ideas

395
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,320
of court of honor scripts online

396
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:02,000
and there are even books about eagle courts of honor.

397
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,760
There's plenty of ideas out there.

398
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,640
I'm saying, keep it simple.

399
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:07,920
And I'm saying this because, having written

400
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:11,160
and directed two plays and acted in many more,

401
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:14,720
I can tell you that dialogue and blocking

402
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:19,140
and scenery and costumes and the theatrical aspects

403
00:22:19,140 --> 00:22:23,160
of staging a play require about two or three people

404
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:27,040
behind the scenes for every person that you see on stage.

405
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:29,160
So what you see from the audience

406
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:32,480
if you go to see a play is just the tip of the iceberg.

407
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:34,200
If you have the resources and energy

408
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:36,640
for an elaborately staged court of honor

409
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:37,720
will more power to you

410
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:39,720
If you wanna change the script every time

411
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,760
and you wanna do it differently.

412
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,000
like I say, more power to you

413
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,680
What you may not know,

414
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:47,080
especially if you're just starting a troupe

415
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:51,600
or have just started your tenure as a scout master.

416
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:54,960
once you've staged a big, elaborate court of honor

417
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,440
and put a lot of energy into it

418
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:58,280
and gotten a lot of people involved in it,

419
00:22:58,320 --> 00:23:01,160
you've set a precedent and you'll be expected

420
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:05,280
to meet the precedent of that big, elaborate court of honor

421
00:23:05,280 --> 00:23:07,320
for all subsequent courts of honor.

422
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,960
That's another aspect of this

423
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:12,280
that kind of recommends simplicity in my mind.

424
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:14,800
I would also suggest that your youth leadership,

425
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,160
led by the senior patrol here,

426
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:18,240
do all the presenting at courts of honor.

427
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:21,639
Our courts of honor are MC'd by our senior patrol leader.

428
00:23:21,639 --> 00:23:23,440
There's no adults up there

429
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:25,960
and he invites me, the scout master,

430
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:28,560
up to the stage to help him present ranks

431
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:31,120
from first class up. but that's my only part in it.

432
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:33,000
Now, while a good court of honor

433
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,840
should have some formality and gravity

434
00:23:35,840 --> 00:23:39,000
commensurate with honoring achievement,

435
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,480
they don't need to be stilted and uncomfortable.

436
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:44,120
There ought to be a lot of smiles

437
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:46,800
and the inevitable mistakes that are made

438
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:49,760
in the presentation should be taken pretty lightly.

439
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:52,840
Nobody gets laughed at, no horrified gasps

440
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,960
from the audience if something goes wrong

441
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:59,520
and no reason for anybody to feel bad or to be embarrassed.

442
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:02,680
But we still wanna maintain that atmosphere

443
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:05,080
that something important is happening.

444
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:06,960
And I do wanna take a moment to talk a little bit

445
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,080
about Eagle Courts of Honor.

446
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:10,880
You know there are folks who insist

447
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,000
that the Eagle Court of Honor

448
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,000
must be a separate presentation

449
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,320
from a normal court of honor.

450
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,080
Some troops have the tradition

451
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,720
of holding separate presentations

452
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,800
for each individual Eagle Scout

453
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:23,720
and some present the Eagle Award

454
00:24:23,760 --> 00:24:28,200
as part of a more or less normal troop court of honor.

455
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:30,800
I can't find any rule to follow about that.

456
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:33,760
I think either way is just fine.

457
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:36,600
Some troops delegate planning the Eagle Court of Honor

458
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,560
to the scout and his family,

459
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,680
And if that works with you, fine.

460
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,760
I think it can lead to problems

461
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:47,760
And I know I say that because it has in the past for me.

462
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:51,520
Some parents lose the distinction

463
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,480
between what an Eagle Court of Honor

464
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:56,960
and a coronation is. okay.

465
00:24:56,960 --> 00:25:01,760
One huge, expensive, theatrical Eagle Court of Honor

466
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:04,320
can set a precedent for the next family

467
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:06,520
to meet or surpass,

468
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:10,760
And soon you may end up with this upward spiral.

469
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:11,880
that's hard to stop

470
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:14,480
And, like I said, I've seen it happen

471
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:17,760
And it can get kind of difficult.

472
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:20,640
So what I mean by that? think about this.

473
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:25,160
Think about a catered reception with a live band. okay,

474
00:25:25,160 --> 00:25:28,880
Does that sound a little over the top?

475
00:25:28,880 --> 00:25:30,400
I've seen it happen.

476
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:32,560
And then that creates the expectation

477
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:35,120
for the next family, who may not be as well to do

478
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:37,280
or may not have the energy or the resources

479
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,240
to put into something like that.

480
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:42,760
And now we're working with a can of worms.

481
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:47,000
Besides those considerations,

482
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,520
I can also tell you from having talked

483
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:53,520
with a lot of Eagle candidates over the years:

484
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:58,520
a lot of them prefer a simple, meaningful, brief-

485
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:03,680
and emphasize the word brief- ceremony

486
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,879
than a really big show. okay,

487
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,240
Some guys they're into the big show

488
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,879
and everything like that. that's fine.

489
00:26:11,879 --> 00:26:14,840
I will tell you that some years ago,

490
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:16,520
after a lot of fuss and bother

491
00:26:16,520 --> 00:26:18,480
and uncomfortable committee meetings

492
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:21,080
and heated arguments and hurt feelings,

493
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:24,520
we finally agreed to hold our Eagle Courts of Honor

494
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:27,600
as a part of our regular troop courts of honor.

495
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:28,920
We make our courts of honor

496
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:31,800
where we're presenting an Eagle Award very, very special.

497
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:34,600
It's not just handing out the Eagle rank

498
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:36,240
as if it was just another rank,

499
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:38,600
but we kind of have a description.

500
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:41,120
that keeps it all pretty simple

501
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:43,880
And thus far everybody's pretty happy about it.

502
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:47,400
I'll say again, we read the resources

503
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,480
and commented a little bit on the resources

504
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:51,920
and then I gave you some of my thoughts,

505
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:54,480
not policy statements or directions,

506
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:57,000
but just my thoughts about the court of honor.

507
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:59,520
So the last step of scout advancement is

508
00:26:59,520 --> 00:27:02,120
a scout is recognized twice.

509
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:04,680
He gets recognized as soon as possible

510
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,440
after all, the paperwork's done

511
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,680
and the badge is in our hands.

512
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:10,400
We make sure that he gets the badge

513
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:13,080
at a simple recognition ceremony

514
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:15,440
at the end of a troop meeting or on a camp out-

515
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:17,040
Doesn't have to be a big deal

516
00:27:17,040 --> 00:27:19,680
And then he gets recognized a second time

517
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,720
more formally at a court of honor,

518
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:23,200
and suggested the courts of honor

519
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,120
should be held about four times a year,

520
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,280
about every three months.

521
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,920
You'll find some links to the resources

522
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:30,040
that we shared here on the post

523
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:33,320
that contains this podcast at scoutmastercgcom.

524
