Oh, be forgiving,

532
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:06,600
Somewhat abusing,

533
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:09,120
For the good Lord.

534
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:12,080
Look for such

535
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:15,200
Dear Roddy's day and smile

536
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,640
On your way.

537
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:20,840
Don't cause very much.

538
00:28:20,840 --> 00:28:23,280
Oh, head down,

539
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:25,720
Cause very much.

540
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:30,800
Where to place the gentle touch

541
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:35,399
To give a glass of water

542
00:28:35,399 --> 00:28:40,320
To a pilgrim in need of sight.

543
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:44,919
Oh, you may not be an angel

544
00:28:44,919 --> 00:28:49,960
And you may not go to church,

545
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:52,760
But the good that you do

546
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:55,120
Will come back to you.

547
00:28:55,160 --> 00:29:02,400
It don't cause very much.

548
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:06,800
Write me a letter,

549
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:08,600
Send it my name,

550
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:12,600
Email, that is, folks.

551
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:15,560
And here's an answer to one of your emails:

552
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:18,560
["To Smile When You're Happy"].

553
00:29:24,560 --> 00:29:27,240
So I've got two email questions that came in this week.

554
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:32,320
Derek Morton is with PAC-780 in Vale, Arizona,

555
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:33,720
and he wrote to say this:

556
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:36,480
Clark, great podcast and blog posts.

557
00:29:36,480 --> 00:29:37,720
I've been listening for some time

558
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:40,480
and I always find myself waiting for the next one.

559
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:43,639
I'm currently a Weebelos 2 den leader.

560
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:47,080
My plan is to start a troop in our local area.

561
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:47,960
I'm an Eagle Scout

562
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,320
and I've been involved in scouting for many, many years,

563
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:52,040
but I've never started a troop.

564
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,280
My question is this:

565
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:57,640
does the BSA have a guide to starting a troop?

566
00:29:57,640 --> 00:30:00,800
I've spoken at length to our council and district

567
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:03,000
and to the commissioners,

568
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,120
but I can't find anything in writing from BSA

569
00:30:05,120 --> 00:30:06,880
on starting a troop.

570
00:30:06,880 --> 00:30:09,040
Searching the internet has produced the same results.

571
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:09,880
What am I missing?

572
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:13,480
Well, first of all, Derek, good on you for stepping up

573
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,160
with the idea of starting a troop.

574
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:16,760
It's a wonderful thing to do.

575
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:18,600
You should be able to get a lot of support

576
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,240
from your district and council folks

577
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:21,800
as you go through the process.

578
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:25,120
The resource that you're looking for actually does exist.

579
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:28,280
It's hiding in plain sight, right.

580
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:29,240
This is what you need.

581
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:31,080
You need a copy of a scout handbook

582
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:32,480
and the scout master handbook,

583
00:30:32,480 --> 00:30:33,880
the troop committee guidebook

584
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:34,960
and something called

585
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:38,040
the Chartered Organization Representative Pamphlet,

586
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:41,360
And I'll link you to a PDF version of that

587
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:44,080
in the post that contains this podcast,

588
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:46,680
Since these resources all correspond

589
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:50,800
to three key people who will get a new troop going.

590
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:52,480
I would get those resources.

591
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:54,000
I would get these three people-

592
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,800
the scout master, the troop committee chair

593
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,840
and the Chartered Organization Representative-

594
00:30:58,840 --> 00:31:01,240
to sit down with all those resources

595
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,760
and start mapping out a plan

596
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:04,320
for the first year of the troop.

597
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:06,560
I promise you'll find all the information

598
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:08,560
that you need in those resources

599
00:31:08,560 --> 00:31:10,160
And by the time you do this

600
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:13,840
you'll be very conversant with those resources

601
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,560
and how things work.

602
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:17,840
I like that idea better

603
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:20,880
than creating a how to start a troop book.

604
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:22,400
I think it's well worth the time

605
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:23,920
to sort it out on your own.

606
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:25,480
Now. you didn't ask me for this advice,

607
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:29,280
but I'm pretty good in offering unsolicited advice.

608
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:31,480
Don't even think about trying to do this by yourself

609
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:33,520
If you don't have those three key people-

610
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:34,920
the scout master, committee chair

611
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,520
and Chartered Organization Representative.

612
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:39,120
get them lined up first

613
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,360
And the three of you get together

614
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:41,920
and make a commitment to each other

615
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:44,280
for at least maybe three years.

616
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:46,480
Don't improvise, don't customize.

617
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:49,400
do it by the book and refine your approach

618
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,720
as time goes by.

619
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,800
Don't sweat the council paperwork.

620
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:55,880
Any district executive worth his salt

621
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,440
will show up on your doorstep

622
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,440
with the correct paperwork

623
00:31:58,440 --> 00:32:00,280
and help you fill it all out.

624
00:32:00,280 --> 00:32:03,200
There's one form for starting a new unit,

625
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:05,080
one form each for the scouts

626
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:07,520
and adults involved. and that's about it

627
00:32:07,520 --> 00:32:08,920
From a paperwork standpoint.

628
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:10,440
it's really very simple.

629
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:12,280
You're gonna have a grand time.

630
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:13,520
Keep in touch, Derek,

631
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:15,360
and let us know how things go

632
00:32:15,360 --> 00:32:17,800
and let us know if we can be of any further insistence.

633
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:20,800
And, once again, thanks for getting in touch.

634
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:23,160
This email question comes from Iowa.

635
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:25,720
How would you approach a scout master

636
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:28,400
that withholds positions of responsibility

637
00:32:28,400 --> 00:32:31,360
from the boys at star and life rank

638
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:32,960
because the scout master contends

639
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:35,200
they do not have scout spirit?

640
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:38,000
Well, first of all, thanks for getting in touch.

641
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,720
I gotta tell you, when I got this email,

642
00:32:39,720 --> 00:32:41,560
I laughed out loud

643
00:32:41,560 --> 00:32:44,480
because my first reaction was:

644
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:46,200
I would approach a scout master doing this,

645
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:48,880
probably with a pointed stick,

646
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:53,600
And oh okay,

647
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:55,400
None of us are going to do that. all right,

648
00:32:55,400 --> 00:32:56,760
I understand,

649
00:32:56,760 --> 00:32:58,800
But that sort of thing is tempting

650
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:01,240
when somebody gets stuff that wrong.

651
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:03,720
I hear about this type of scout master

652
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:04,760
on a regular basis.

653
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:08,160
So let's talk about a few ideas to handle this.

654
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:10,480
Assuming that the person who sent me this email,

655
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:12,040
their son, is a scout,

656
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:13,879
They've been told by the scout master

657
00:33:13,879 --> 00:33:16,879
that they are lacking in scout spirit

658
00:33:16,879 --> 00:33:20,120
And that lack of scout spirit disqualifies them

659
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:22,320
for a position of responsibility.

660
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:26,640
And since the email mentions both star and life ranks.

661
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:28,560
I get the impression that this scout master

662
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:30,080
has a habit of doing this.

663
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:31,600
He's wrong,

664
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:33,080
And he's wrong in several ways.

665
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:36,440
Most importantly, he's wrong about this

666
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:38,480
because he hasn't read or remembered

667
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:40,640
what's in the scout master's handbook.

668
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,800
One of the things you'll find there

669
00:33:41,800 --> 00:33:44,280
is that the positions of the senior patrol leader

670
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:47,560
and patrol leader are democratically elected

671
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:48,720
by the scouts.

672
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:51,920
The troop can set some very basic expectations

673
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:53,320
to qualify for the election.

674
00:33:53,320 --> 00:33:56,520
These may be age, or they may be rank

675
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:57,880
or something like that.

676
00:33:57,880 --> 00:34:01,600
I would never, ever set a judgment call

677
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:03,960
kind of thing where the scout master

678
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:07,240
then becomes the gatekeeper for who gets to stand

679
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:10,720
for election. like a scout spirit,

680
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:13,080
I just would recommend against that.

681
00:34:13,080 --> 00:34:15,120
Every other position of responsibility

682
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:17,760
other than junior assistant scout master

683
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:20,880
is appointed by the senior patrol leader,

684
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:22,280
And the exact wording you find

685
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,880
in the scout master handbook is this:

686
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:26,680
Depending on the size and needs of a troop,

687
00:34:26,680 --> 00:34:29,960
any or all of the following positions may be filled,

688
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:32,280
And then it goes on to list those positions.

689
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:35,600
Unless indicated, the senior patrol leader

690
00:34:35,600 --> 00:34:38,679
selects the scout who will hold each position.

691
00:34:38,679 --> 00:34:43,679
The scout master can help, can help, can not must.

692
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:47,520
He can help the senior patrol leader

693
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:49,920
make his decisions on the basis

694
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:54,159
of candidates overall qualifications

695
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:56,560
rather than merely on friendships.

696
00:34:56,560 --> 00:34:58,560
So our problem scout master here

697
00:34:58,560 --> 00:35:01,160
is trying to become the gatekeeper

698
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:04,600
and impose judgment where it really doesn't belong.

699
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:07,480
Some of the youth leaders are elected democratically

700
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:09,160
and some of them are appointed

701
00:35:09,160 --> 00:35:10,759
by the senior patrol leader,

702
00:35:10,759 --> 00:35:13,680
So this is a youth based decision.

703
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:16,080
He's also missed the fact that we motivate

704
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:18,720
and support our scouts by responding

705
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:21,320
to and enabling their aspirations,

706
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:24,759
not by keeping them from those aspirations.

707
00:35:24,759 --> 00:35:28,440
I'll tell you very clearly that I've had doubts

708
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:32,280
about a scout's suitability and ability

709
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:34,920
to take on a position of responsibility,

710
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:38,640
But my job is to encourage and motivate him

711
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:39,760
to do the best he can,

712
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:42,240
Not just to say, hey, I don't think you're up to this,

713
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:44,440
so forget about it, right?

714
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:46,160
Some of my best youth leaders

715
00:35:46,160 --> 00:35:48,160
were really shaking and uncertain at first

716
00:35:48,160 --> 00:35:50,720
and a lot of times all they needed

717
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:53,400
was someone to believe in them

718
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:56,600
and that they had the capacity to do the job.

719
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:59,880
How can anybody think that telling a boy

720
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:01,240
you know you don't qualify

721
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:02,839
because you don't have enough scout spirit

722
00:36:02,839 --> 00:36:05,080
is going to motivate or encourage them

723
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,720
to have more scout spirit?

724
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:11,080
If I was a boy and somebody told me something like that,

725
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:13,720
I think I would turn around, walk away and never come back.

726
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:15,480
We know that what you're telling us

727
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:17,960
the scout master is doing sounds wrong.

728
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:20,440
So what do you do about something like this?

729
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:24,360
Well, it's really not up to you alone.

730
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:26,120
This is up to your scout.

731
00:36:26,160 --> 00:36:28,279
He ought to educate himself a little bit

732
00:36:28,279 --> 00:36:30,040
by reading a scout handbook,

733
00:36:30,040 --> 00:36:33,359
and even looking at the scout master handbook,

734
00:36:33,359 --> 00:36:35,839
about how these things are supposed to work.

735
00:36:35,839 --> 00:36:37,720
and then he ought to stand up for himself

736
00:36:37,720 --> 00:36:39,319
and go to the scout master and say:

737
00:36:39,319 --> 00:36:41,799
you know, I really don't understand

738
00:36:41,799 --> 00:36:43,480
why you're preventing me

739
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:46,319
from taking on a position of responsibility.

740
00:36:46,319 --> 00:36:48,960
If a number of scouts get together and do this,

741
00:36:48,960 --> 00:36:51,640
that scout master just may change his tune.

742
00:36:51,640 --> 00:36:54,799
Now, this requires some backbone

743
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,080
and some hutzpah

744
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:58,840
and it requires a scout to be brave,

745
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:01,480
but it would be a very, very good thing

746
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:03,360
for him to be able to do

747
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:05,080
Now. if they give this a shot

748
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:07,280
and they don't get anywhere, then,

749
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:10,120
and only then, I think it's time for parents

750
00:37:10,120 --> 00:37:12,720
to get together and to go to the scout master

751
00:37:12,720 --> 00:37:14,960
and ask him to explain why he's doing what he's doing

752
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:17,400
and how he justifies what he is doing

753
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:19,040
according to his training.

754
00:37:19,040 --> 00:37:20,840
If the parents don't get what they consider

755
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:22,680
to be a reasonable explanation,

756
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:25,839
then I would get the parents and the sons together

757
00:37:25,839 --> 00:37:28,080
and I would talk about finding another troop

758
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:31,040
who, scout master, understands the program

759
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:33,720
and then you vote with your feet

760
00:37:33,720 --> 00:37:36,319
on the suitability of that scout master.

761
00:37:36,319 --> 00:37:38,279
I don't think it's necessarily a great idea

762
00:37:38,279 --> 00:37:40,120
to try and change the troop,

763
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:42,240
and I don't really know from this email

764
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:45,040
what all the extenuating factors are

765
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:46,480
about this particular troop.

766
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:48,160
I don't know how long this scout master

767
00:37:48,160 --> 00:37:49,960
has been around or the relationship he has

768
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,279
with the troop committee,

769
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:53,240
If the troop committee is a paper committee

770
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:54,840
or if it's actually functioning,

771
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:59,240
what kind of shape the chartered partner relationship is in.

772
00:38:00,240 --> 00:38:03,440
Maybe the best thing to do in this case

773
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:07,400
is to find out who the commissioner for the troop is

774
00:38:07,400 --> 00:38:09,200
and ask their advice.

775
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:10,520
I will tell you two things

776
00:38:10,520 --> 00:38:12,960
that I would prefer no one do

777
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:15,200
when they're in this kind of a situation.

778
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:19,400
One is to hold conversations

779
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:24,400
or make accusations or do anything by email.

780
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:26,720
When you're confronting this type of a problem,

781
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,120
you better do it all face to face,

782
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:30,360
and here's why

783
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:33,200
People will say things in email

784
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:36,000
that they would never say in person.

785
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:39,160
Email's not contextualized by standing there

786
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:40,320
and talking to a person

787
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:43,280
and hearing the tone of their words

788
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:45,920
and seeing the expression on their face

789
